    <briefdescription>
<para>An interface for accessing data in a stream-like format, but which discourages copying. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Instead of specifying a buffer in which to copy data on a read, the API returns an <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_array_ref" kindref="compound">ArrayRef</ref> to data owned by the stream&apos;s implementation. Since implementations may not necessarily store data in a single contiguous buffer (or even in memory at all), in such cases a it may be necessary for an implementation to cache such a buffer so that it can return it. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
